  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building for Community and Social Organisations in Vietnam: Gender Mainstreaming in Development Programmes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the capacity of community and social organisations in Vietnam in Hanoi, HCMC and other provinces by providing essential training and networking opportunities. Specifically, the project will: 

 

Organise one training sessions for 35 individuals and organizations in HCMC, focusing on gender mainstreaming, including foundational gender concepts and strategies to address gender-related issues  

Conduct one learning and exchanging seminar for individuals from Hanoi cohort and HCMC cohort to facilitate the sharing of lessons on gender mainstreaming in project design, implementation, and management. 

Host a networking reception in collaboration with the British Embassy for 45 individuals from NGOs, CBOs and business sectors (invited by the embassy) from Hanoi and HCMC, providing further opportunities for networking and collaboration.</narrative>
  </description>
